      "id": 4,
      "question": "A 46-year-old man presents with diarrhoea and persistent abdominal cramps. This has not affected his appetite, which has increased without weight gain. Upon further questioning he reports that he went on a safari holiday in Kenya two months ago where he consumed undercooked pork. The patient has brought in a stool sample from which you can see a small white thread-like structure protruding.\n\n\nWBC\t10.1 * 109/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\nNeuts\t5.4 * 109/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nLymphs\t3.0 * 109/L\t(1.0 - 3.5)\nMono\t0.6 * 109/L\t(0.2 - 0.8)\nEosin\t1.1 * 109/L\t(0.0 - 0.4)\n\nWhat cell is responsible for producing the immunoglobulin implicated in this patient's presentation?",
