      "id": 24,
      "question": "A 19-year-old man is referred to neurology with a 2-year history of progressive gait disturbance and clumsiness. He has no significant past medical history. His parents are unaffected, but his younger sister has similar symptoms. On examination, he has dysarthria, absent ankle reflexes, and extensor plantar responses. Echocardiogram shows concentric left ventricular hypertrophy. Genetic testing confirms a GAA trinucleotide repeat expansion.\n\nWhat is the most likely inheritance pattern of this condition?",
