      "explanation": "The fastest conduction velocities in the heart are in the Purkinje fibres\n\nA prolonged QRS (>120ms) with a dominant S wave in V1 is suggestive of left bundle branch block (LBBB). In the context of chest pain, a raised troponin, and a previously normal ECG, then the patient should be managed as an acute STEMI. LBBB occurs due to damage of the left bundle branch and associated\n\nPurkinje fibres\n\n.\n\nInfarction of the\n\nSA node\n\nand\n\nAV node\n\ncan also occur due to myocardial infarction. However, they would present with bradycardia and heart block.\n\nThe\n\nInteratrial pathway\n\nand\n\nInternodal pathway\n\nare part of the atrial conduction system. Infarction of the atria would not cause LBBB."
