      "correctText": "Meta-analysis decreases power and decreases p value",
      "explanation": "Meta-analysis increases power and improves estimates of the size of the effect by combining individual studies that may be low-powered\n\nPower is the probability of rejecting the null hypothesis ('there is no difference') given the null is false (there\n\nactually\n\nis a difference) - you would want to reject the null if it was false. Meta-analysis combines multiple studies and\n\nincreases power\n\ni.e. you are more likely to be correct in your rejection of the null.\n\nThe p-value is the probability that we reject the null hypothesis (we say there is a difference) while it is true (there\n\nactually\n\nis no difference) - i.e. the probability of incorrectly rejecting the null, so its good to have a small p-value. Meta-analysis combines multiple studies and improves the probability of correctly rejecting the null, thus\n\ndecreasing the p-value\n\n."
