      "id": 58,
      "question": "A 45-year-old man with a BMI of 41 kg/m² presents to the clinic complaining of persistent hunger and difficulty losing weight, despite making dietary changes and exercising regularly. He has no history of diabetes or thyroid disease.\n\nWhat adipose tissue-derived hormone is this patient most likely resistant to, contributing to his condition?",
