      "question": "A 30-year-old man is reviewed in the congenital cardiology clinic. He has cardiomyopathy secondary to an inherited lysosomal storage disorder which was diagnosed in childhood with genetic testing. He initially presented with acute pain crisis of his hands and feet, reduced sweating, corneal opacities and angiokeratomas. He now takes enzyme replacement therapy.\n\nWhat is the inheritance pattern of the underlying condition?",
