      "question": "A 20-year-old woman presents to the ophthalmology department, with blurred vision in her right eye. She is noted to have a marfanoid body type and a degree of learning difficulties. Her past medical history includes epilepsy and a previous deep vein thrombosis (DVT).\n\nOn slit lamp examination, the upper edge of an inferiorly displaced subluxated lens can be seen.\n\nWhat is the underlying diagnosis?",
