      "explanation": "Odds -  remember a ratio of the number of people who incur a particular outcome to the number of people who do not incur the outcome\n\n8/1000\n\nis the correct answer. The odds of a particular event (in this case developing thyroid cancer when exposed to ionizing ratio) is a ratio of the number of people who incur a particular outcome to the number of people who do not incur a particular outcome. When exposed to ionizing radiation, 8 people develop thyroid cancer and 1000 do not therefore the ratio is 8/1000.\n\n(8/1000)/(6/5635)\n\nis incorrect. This formula describes the odds ratio, which is a way to present the strength of association between exposures and outcomes.\n\n6/5635\n\nis incorrect. This is the odds of developing thyroid cancer in the population not exposed to ionising radiation.\n\n6/5641\n\nis incorrect. This is the incidence of thyroid cancer in non-exposed individuals rather than the odds i.e. the total number of cases as a proportion of the total non-exposed population.\n\n8/1008\n\nis incorrect. This is the incidence of thyroid cancer in the total exposed population."
