      "question": "A 30-year-old man presents to clinic. He has fine, fair hair and long arms. He has visible kyphosis and mild learning difficulties. He has had seizures in the past. He has previously been reviewed by ophthalmology due to downward dislocation of his lens and severe myopia. He has also been reviewed in haematology clinic with recurrent deep vein thrombosis.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
