      "question": "A 16-year-old girl is referred to the cardiology clinic for assessment. She has a history of primary amenorrhoea, short stature, and a webbed neck. She has no cardiac symptoms. On examination, she has widely spaced nipples and a systolic murmur. An echocardiogram is performed.\n\nWhat is the most likely cardiac abnormality?",
