      "question": "A 7-year-old girl with sensorineural deafness and retinitis pigmentosa is reviewed in a paediatric genetics clinic.\n\nGenetic sequencing reveals a pathological variant of the MYO7A gene. This single-nucleotide substitution is associated with Usher syndrome, producing a truncated and nonfunctioning myosin VIIa protein. Further analysis shows that the substitution mutation creates a premature stop codon.\n\nWhat type of mutation is likely present?",
