      "question": "A 44-year-old woman was referred to the rheumatology clinic with a 4-month history of persistent lethargy, breathlessness, and pain in her shoulders, hands, and feet. On examination, there is a rash over her nose and cheeks. Urine is positive for both blood and protein. The rheumatology consultant decides to order some blood tests including complement levels.\n\nGiven the most likely diagnosis, which complement is likely to be deficient?",
