      "question": "A 43-year-old woman presents with lethargy, bony pain, and proximal muscle weakness. She has no underlying co-morbidities. Blood tests are consistent with osteomalacia and you prescribe vitamin D supplementation.\n\nWhat is the primary mechanism by which this treatment increases serum calcium?",
