      "explanation": "Power = 1 - the probability of a type II error\n\nReality\tH1\tH0\nStudy rejects H0\tPower (1-Beta)\tAlpha (Type I error)\nStudy does not reject H0\tBeta (Type II error)\t-\n\nPower means correctly identifying the result regardless of whether the hypothesis is accepted or rejected. A study with high power can accurately identify an effect or difference when one exists or vice versa.\n\nPower = 1 - the probability of a type II error.\n\nPower = 1 - 0.26 = 0.74\n\nWhen the probability of type II error of a study decreases, the power increases."
