      "question": "A 28-year-old female with a background of Crohn's disease presents to her general practitioner complaining of general fatigue and shortness of breath on exertion.\n\nShe was recently discharged from hospital after a flare of her inflammatory bowel disease, but symptoms are now controlled after being commenced on azathioprine.\n\nRoutine bloods are arranged and results show :\n\n\n\nHb\t106 g/L\tMale: (135-180)\nFemale: (115 - 160)\nPlatelets\t184 * 109/L\t(150 - 400)\nWBC\t5.6 * 109/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\n\n\nESR\t5 mm/hr\tMen: < (age / 2)\nWomen: < ((age + 10) / 2)\nProthrombin time (PT)\t11.6 secs\t(10-14 secs)\nActivated partial thromboplastin time (APTT)\t29 secs\t(25-35 secs)\nFibrinogen\t3.2 g/L\t(2 - 4)\nD-Dimer\t20 ng/mL\t(< 400)\nFerritin\t8 ng/mL\t(20 - 230)\nVitamin B12\t461 ng/L\t(200 - 900)\nFolate\t6.4 nmol/L\t(> 3.0)\nReticulocytes\t0.9 %\t(0.5 - 1.5)\n\nGiven her blood results, she is commenced on appropriate replacement therapy.\n\nWhich of the following supplements would improve her response to treatment?",
