      "question": "A 45-year-old man presents to his general practitioner with several months of pain around the mouth. Specifically, he describes cracking, itching and crusting at the corners of the mouth. He has no significant past medical history and takes no regular medication.\n\nOn examination, significant fissuring and crusting is noted at the angles of the mouth.\n\nWhat deficiency is most likely to be causing his symptoms?",
