      "id": 271,
      "question": "A 33-year-old female has been referred urgently to the breast clinic after noticing an irregular, firm lump in one of her breasts.\n\nOn further enquiry, she reports that she has multiple relatives who were diagnosed with cancer at a relatively young age. Her sister was diagnosed with rhabdomyosarcoma when she was 13 years old, while her mother died of breast cancer in her 40s. Her maternal uncle was also diagnosed with adrenocortical carcinoma.\n\nWhich genetic syndrome accounts for these presentations?",
