      "question": "A 28-year-old man presents to the rheumatology clinic following a referral from his GP for joint pains. He has no significant past medical history but describes experiencing pain and stiffness in the small joints of his hands, along with lower back discomfort. His GP is concurrently investigating him for unexplained diarrhoea.\n\nDuring the physical examination, he exhibits tenderness over all distal interphalangeal joints, accompanied by nail pitting and onycholysis.\n\nWhat is most likely to be positive in this patient?",
