      "correctText": "The value of Box C",
      "explanation": "Power - the probability of detecting a statistically significant difference\n\nThe correct answer is 'The value of Box D'. The power of a study is the probability of correctly rejecting the null hypothesis when it is false.\n\nThe table below shows the possible outcomes of a study (accepting/rejecting the null hypothesis  H\n\n0\n\nin relation to reality - whether the H\n\n0\n\nis true or not.\n\nStudy accepts H0\tStudy rejects H0\nReality H0\t\tType 1 error (alpha)\nReality H1\tType 2 error (beta)\tPower (1-beta)\n\nAlpha (α) and beta (β) are set by the study designers then a calculation of the required study sample size can be done using the difference between groups that the study is trying to detect. The typical level of α is 0.05, which represents a 5% probability of a type 1 error (rejecting the null hypothesis when it is in fact correct).\n\nβ is the probability of a type II error (accepting the null hypothesis when it is in fact incorrect). β is typically set at 0.8.\n\nβ and power sum to 1. Therefore power = 1 - β. Power could be described as '1 - the value of Box C', which is the same as saying power = 1 - the probability of a type II error.\n\nThe statement 'power = 1 + the value of Box D' would be incorrect."
