      "question": "A 58-year-old man with a history of ischemic heart disease is being considered for statin therapy for secondary prevention. A recent large randomised controlled trial showed that statins reduce the risk of major cardiovascular events by 2% over 5 years compared to placebo. The absolute risk of a cardiovascular event in this population without treatment is 10% over 5 years.\n\nWhat best represents the number needed to treat (NNT) with statins to prevent one cardiovascular event over 5 years?",
