      "question": "A 32-year-old man is admitted following a head injury sustained after falling from a horse. A CT head is performed which shows a large extra-dural haematoma causing midline shift and signs of cerebral oedema. He has a reduced GCS with abnormal posturing.\n\nWhich vital signs would be consistent with this presentation?",
