      "correctIndex": 0,
      "correctText": "28%",
      "explanation": "Specificity = TN / (TN + FP)\n\nSpecificity = TN / (TN + FP).\n\nTrue negative is 106 (the number of people without the disease who tested negative). False positive is 54 (the number of people without the disease who tested positive).\n\nSpecificity = 106 / (106 + 54) = 0.6625 = 66%.\n\n28% is the sensitivity of the test, which is the proportion of patients with the condition who have a positive test result. Sensitivity = TP / (TP + FN ) = 40 / (40 + 105) = 0.2759 = 28%."
