      "explanation": "Insulin binds to a receptor tyrosine kinase in the cell membrane\n\nInsulin binds to\n\ntyrosine kinase receptors\n\n. Tyrosine kinase receptors are seen with insulin, insulin-like growth factor, and epidermal growth factor.\n\nBeta-1 receptors\n\nare types of G protein-coupled receptors and they are what epinephrine binds to.\n\nG protein-coupled receptors\n\ngenerally, mediate slow transmission and affect metabolic processes. They are activated by a wide variety of extracellular signals, for example, adrenaline.\n\nGuanylate cyclase receptors\n\ncontain intrinsic enzyme activity and are associated with atrial natriuretic factor and brain natriuretic peptide.\n\nLigand-gated ion channel receptors\n\ngenerally mediate fast responses such as nicotinic acetylcholine."
