      "explanation": "Power - the probability of (correctly) rejecting the null hypothesis when it is false\n\nPower is the probability of (correctly) rejecting the null hypothesis when it is false. It is the probability of not making a type II error.\n\nThe positive predictive value is the probability that subjects with a positive screening test truly have the disease. The negative predictive value is a probability that subjects with a negative screening test truly don't have the disease.\n\nSpecificity is the proportion of patients without the condition who have a negative test result.\n\nA type I error, also known as a false positive, occurs when a researcher incorrectly rejects a true null hypothesis.\n\nA type II error, also known as a false negative, occurs when a researcher incorrectly accepts a false null hypothesis."
