      "id": 358,
      "question": "A 34-year-old woman with severe rheumatoid arthritis is enrolled in a phase I clinical trial investigating a novel targeted therapy. The experimental drug is designed to modulate B-cell function by binding to a specific membrane-bound immunoglobulin that forms part of the B-cell receptor complex.\n\nThis surface immunoglobulin is co-expressed with another isotype on naïve B-cells and is thought to have distinct signalling properties that may enable more selective immunomodulation.\n\nWhat membrane-bound immunoglobulin is this experimental therapy most likely targeting?",
