      "id": 365,
      "question": "A 16-year-old boy is referred for investigation following the development of several organ dysfunctions including chronic kidney disease and congestive heart failure, associated with symptoms of all-over body pain and small painless papules appearing mainly on the child's upper legs.\n\nFabry disease, a lysosomal storage condition, is suspected and confirmed via enzyme assay testing. Given the advancement of his condition, it is recommended the child is started on enzyme replacement therapy immediately.\n\nHow is this condition inherited?",
