      "id": 371,
      "question": "A 45-year-old man attends your clinic. He is concerned as his father has just been diagnosed with Huntington's disease. He is aware that this is a genetic condition and wants to be tested. He also wants more information about the likely course of the condition. You explain that, if he tests positive, he will likely develop symptoms earlier than his father did.\n\nWhat aspect of the condition gives rise to this phenomenon?",
