      "question": "A 35-year-old man complains of a sore throat. Viral pharyngitis is the most likely diagnosis. He is adamant that he requires antibiotics. The data behind their efficacy in sore throats is discussed with him and when compared to placebo, antibiotics show a 2% absolute risk reduction in the rate of complications.\n\nHow can this be expressed to the patient in terms of the number of people that need to be treated in order to get a benefit from antibiotics?",
