      "question": "You are developing a blood test to help diagnose deep vein thrombosis.\n\nThe results of the trial are as follows:\n\n\n\tDisease present\tDisease absent\nTest positive\t12\t162\nTest negative\t3\t1960\n\nYou calculate a key statistical result as (true positive) / (true positive + false positive) = 12 / (12 + 162) = 6.9%.\n\nWhat is this defining?",
