      "question": "A 19-year-old man is referred to the dermatology clinic with a three-month history of raised red spots around his upper lip, abdomen, and upper thighs. In addition, he reports burning in the hands and feet, aggravated by exercise. He has a history of cramping abdominal pain, intolerance to heat, and depression. His urine is positive for proteinuria. The enzyme activity of alpha-galactosidase is reduced on serum testing. His parents are well, and there is no history of genetic disease on the paternal side. A lysosomal storage disorder is suspected.\n\nWhat is the inheritance pattern for this condition?",
