      "question": "A 63-year-old woman with known hypertension, diabetes and high cholesterol presents to the hospital with crushing central chest pain radiating to the jaw. She has vomited twice and reports feeling dizzy.\n\nAn ECG confirms widespread ST elevation with reciprocal ST-segment depression. A troponin T serum level is measured and confirmed to be raised.\n\nThe patient is started on aspirin, morphine and an antiemetic and transferred urgently to a cardiac centre.\n\nWhat does this measured cardiac biomarker bind to?",
