      "question": "A 23-year-old student was brought in from his university residence halls by his concerned friends. They reported that he had complained of a headache and photophobia yesterday, but his condition has deteriorated rapidly in the last 24 hours.\n\nOn examination, he is confused, has a stiff neck, and presents a petechiae rash all over his body. A lumbar puncture confirmed the presence of a gram-negative bacterium with a polysaccharide capsule.\n\nWhat complement component deficiency or deficiencies predispose individuals to this likely infection?",
