      "question": "A 21-year-old university student presents to the emergency department with a headache, fever and confusion, which have been going on since last night. She also complains of neck stiffness and a new rash that has developed over the same time period. Her past medical history is unremarkable except for a known complement deficiency.\n\nOn examination, she appears unwell. Nuchal rigidity and photophobia are present. The patient also has visible truncal petechiae. Observations show pyrexia, tachycardia and hypotension.\n\nWhich complement deficiency is typically associated with the likely diagnosis?",
