      "explanation": "Positive predictive value = TP / (TP + FP)\n\nThe positive predictive value is the number of true positive readings divided by the total number of positive readings.\n\nIn this instance, there were 60 positive tests which turned out to be true as the patient was diagnosed with coronavirus. There were 100 positive readings overall which include 40 positive tests where the patients then were not found to have coronavirus. If you divide the true test results by the total you produce a positive predictive value of 0.6 (60%)."
