      "question": "A 40-year-old man is seen in the nephrology clinic. He has a diagnosis of end-stage renal disease as a result of glomerulonephritis as a child. He and the doctor are discussing the possibility of a renal transplant. The patient is reluctant because he suffered from rejection of a previous kidney transplant attempt abroad while it was being implanted.\n\nWhat cell type is most implicated in this type of organ rejection?",
