      "question": "A 33-year-old patient presents with fever and dysuria to the emergency department. She has no past medical history.\n\nObservations:\n\n\nHeart 131 beats per minute\nBlood pressure 77/44 mmHg\nOxygen saturation 97% on room air\nRespiratory rate 22 / minute\nTemperature 38.8C\n\nOn examination, she is peripheral warm to touch with a bounding pulse. She has lower abdominal tenderness.\n\nWhat is the principal cause of hypotension in this context?",
