      "question": "A 24-year-old man presents with a swollen, itchy right eyelid. This has been ongoing for 10 days but the patient reports it has happened at least 5 times previously. Each time it self-resolved.\n\nOn examination, there is erythema of the anterior lid margin and the base of the lashes of the right eye. Visual acuity, fundoscopy and cranial nerve examination are normal.\n\nYou perform a systematic enquiry to elicit an underlying cause of this recurrent condition.\n\nWhat is the most likely underlying condition?",
