      "question": "A 54-year-old man is referred by his GP to the dermatology outpatient department due to a facial rash which has persisted for the past 12 months. On examination there is a symmetrical rash consisting of extensive pustules and papules which affects his nose, cheeks and forehead. What is the most appropriate treatment?",
