      "question": "A 54-year-old woman attends the dermatology clinic with a 3-month history of an intensely itchy rash on her wrists and ankles. Examination reveals multiple flat-topped, violaceous papules with fine white lines over their surface. She also reports mild discomfort in her mouth. On inspection, there are reticulated white patterns on the buccal mucosa but no ulceration. Which is the most appropriate initial management for her skin findings?",
