      "question": "A 26-year-old woman presents to her GP for lesions on her arms which appeared suddenly several days ago. Her mother persuaded her to attend the appointment - the patient herself was not keen. When asked about the lesions, she does not give a clear history of their appearance/progression. Her past medical history includes mild asthma, depression and generalised anxiety disorder.\n\nOn examination, she has linear, well-demarcated skin lesions on both arms. They do not appear dry or scaly. They appear excoriated. There are no obvious signs of infection.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis for this patient?",
