      "question": "A 38-year-old man presents to his general practitioner with recurrent nosebleeds. He has no past medical history. His mother also suffered from recurrent nosebleeds.\n\nOn examination, he has telangiectasia visible at the lips, hands and nose.\n\nBlood tests:\n\n\nHb\t101 g/L\tMale: (135-180)\n\nHe undergoes a CT chest, abdomen and pelvis, which demonstrates a hepatic arteriovenous malformation.\n\nWhat is the inheritance pattern of the likely underlying diagnosis?",
