      "id": 176,
      "question": "A 20-year-old man presents with a several-month history of lesions on the face. He has a past medical history of recurrent epistaxis since childhood. He is unaware of his biological family history, having been adopted at birth.\n\nOn examination, numerous telangiectasias are noted on the face, lips, tongue and inside the mouth. He is subsequently referred to specialists for further investigations:\n\n\nEndoscopy\tSeveral telangiectasias in the stomach and duodenum\nCT chest, abdomen and pelvis\tNumerous hepatic arteriovenous malformations\n\nWhat is the mode of inheritance of the underlying condition?",
