      "id": 201,
      "question": "A 70-year-old woman with no significant past medical history was found by her GP to have an asymptomatic tan-brown patch located on her left temple which was 22 mm in diameter. The lesion has been slowly growing into an elevated nodule over the last five years. She reports a lifestyle that has involved a significant amount of sunlight exposure.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis in this case?",
