      "id": 234,
      "question": "A 24-year-old woman with a background of acne vulgaris has been referred to the clinic due to a flare of her acne causing scarring and hyperpigmentation. She is 14 weeks pregnant with her first child and thinks this may have triggered the flare. She has used tretinoin and doxycycline to manage her skin successfully in the past but changed to her current regime of topical benzoyl peroxide with topical clindamycin 6 months ago as she wanted to conceive.\n\nWhat is the most appropriate treatment option in this case?",
