      "question": "A 25-year-old woman presents to her GP with scaly, discoloured patches on her chest and back. She reports that these patches become more pronounced after sun exposure and are accompanied by mild itching. Physical examination reveals multiple hypopigmented, well-demarcated patches with fine scaling.\n\nWhat is the most appropriate treatment option for this patient?",
