      "id": 3,
      "question": "A 39-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with oily rectal discharge, excessive flatulence, and an urgent need to open her bowels shortly after eating. These symptoms began two weeks after starting a new weight loss medication.\n\nWhat is the mechanism of action of the medication most likely responsible for her symptoms?",
