      "id": 9,
      "question": "A 32-year-old woman attends the endocrinology clinic with fatigue and constipation. She has a history of menorrhagia, Wolff-Parkinson-White syndrome, and primary hypothyroidism. Her thyroid function tests were satisfactory 6 months ago. Her drug history includes levothyroxine 100 micrograms (once daily at 7am), amiodarone 200mg (once daily at 7am), and ferrous fumarate 210mg (once daily at 7am).\n\nBlood results are as follows:\n\n\nThyroid stimulating hormone (TSH)\t24.2 mU/L\t(0.5-5.5)\nFree thyroxine (T4)\t6.8 pmol/L\t(9.0 - 18)\n\nHow will you manage this situation?",
