      "id": 28,
      "question": "A 72-year-old man is reviewed in the diabetes clinic. He has a history of heart failure and type 2 diabetes mellitus. His current medications include furosemide 40mg od, ramipril 10mg od and bisoprolol 5mg od. Clinical examination is unremarkable with no evidence of peripheral oedema, a clear chest and blood pressure of 130/76 mmHg. Recent renal and liver function tests are normal. Which one of the following medications is contraindicated?",
