      "question": "A 45-year-old man presents to the endocrinology outpatient clinic with complaints of increasing shoe size and coarsening facial features over the past year. He also reports headaches and joint pain. His serum insulin-like growth factor 1 (IGF-1) levels are found to be elevated.\n\nWhich is the most appropriate next step in confirming the diagnosis?",
