      "id": 63,
      "question": "A 40-year-old woman presents to her GP with discomfort in her anterior neck that she describes as a slight tightness. She does not complain of dysphagia or a hoarse voice.\n\nOn examination, she has a diffuse neck goitre that is hard on palpation, non-tender and fixed in position.\n\nWhat other finding is most likely in this patient?",
