      "id": 89,
      "question": "A 60-year-old man is admitted to the endocrine ward following a one-month history of polyuria and polydipsia, he appears severely dehydrated. A water deprivation test is performed which shows the following result.\n\n\nUrine osmolality post-fluid deprivation\t50mOsm/kg\t(50-1200)\nUrine osmolality post-desmopressin\t700mOsm/kg\t(50-1200)\n\nWhat is the diagnosis?",
