      "question": "A 23-year-old student presents to his new GP in the UK to arrange ongoing follow-up for a genetic condition. The patient states that his father died from bowel cancer in his 30s.\n\nThe patient states that genetic testing was performed whilst he was a child which led to yearly colonoscopies starting aged 10 and eventually, he had a total colectomy and ileoanal pouch formation 2 years ago in the US. He states that he now has upper endoscopies yearly.\n\nWhat gene mutation is associated with the most likely underlying diagnosis?",
