      "id": 55,
      "question": "A 55-year-old man presents to the emergency department with progressive abdominal swelling and no significant past medical history. On examination, his abdomen is distended and shifting dullness is present. Fluid aspiration from his abdomen and subsequent blood tests reveal the following results:\n\n\nSerum albumin\t31 g/L\nAscites albumin\t11 g/L\n\nWhat is the most likely cause of his presentation?",
