      "question": "A 45-year-old man presents to the GP with a 3-month history of diarrhoea. The patient states that he has lost weight and his clothes feel baggier, although he is not sure how much he has lost. On further questioning, he discloses that he has had pain in both of his knees for a similar period of time, and for the last couple of days he has suffered blurred vision on the extremes of his vision. On examination, widespread lymphadenopathy is noted.\n\nWhat is the most likely underlying cause?",
