      "id": 75,
      "question": "A 40-year-old woman with a family history of multiple endocrine neoplasia type 1 presents to her GP with upper abdominal pain. She reports that she has experienced worsening dyspepsia after meals for the last three months. On wider questioning, she reveals that for this period, her stools have been loose, and she has lost around a stone in weight unintentionally.\n\nWhat is the normal physiological role of the hormone responsible for this patient's presentation?",
