      "explanation": "Clostridioides difficile\n\nFaecal-oral route by ingestion of spores\n\nis correct. The patient most likely has\n\nC. difficile\n\ninfection due to the recent history of ciprofloxacin.  This infection spreads via the faecal-oral route by ingestion of spores.\n\nAerosol\n\nis incorrect.  Aerosol transmission is the transmission of an infectious disease through small particles suspended in the air. Examples include measles, varicella zoster, and influenza virus.\n\nDroplet\n\nis incorrect. Respiratory droplet transmission is the usual route for respiratory infections. Common pathogens spread by droplet transmission include influenza virus, rhinovirus, respiratory syncytial virus, enterovirus, and norovirus.\n\nFaecal-oral route by ingestion of bacteria\n\nis incorrect.\n\nC.difficile\n\nspreads via the ingestion of spores.\n\nWaterborne\n\nis incorrect. Cholera, typhoid fever, dysentery, and hepatitis A and E, are examples of waterborne diseases."
