      "id": 82,
      "question": "A 70-year-old is seen on the ward after originally being admitted for a chest infection requiring several courses of antibiotics.\n\nAfter the last course, the patient's respiratory symptoms improved however they developed diarrhoea with a stool sample testing positive for Clostridium difficile and so they were started on a course of oral vancomycin.\n\nToday is day 10 of the vancomycin but the patient still reports diarrhoea and abdominal cramps. Observations and investigations today are:\n\n\nHeart rate 102/min\nBP 130/80 mmHg\nOxygen saturations 96% on air\nTemperature 38.1 oC\n\n\nWCC\t15x109/L\t4.5-11\nAbdominal x-ray\tEvidence of colitis\t\n\nWhat treatment should be started now?",
