      "question": "A 46-year-old woman with 10 year history of Crohn's disease presents for review in the gastroenterology clinic. She complains of persistent diarrhoea despite being on maintenance therapy and having normal inflammatory markers. A diagnosis of bile acid malabsorption is being considered. What is the most appropriate test to investigate this?",
