      "id": 106,
      "question": "A 52-year-old originally presents with frequent, on-off epigastric discomfort and burning, radiating up to the throat, commonly associated with certain food types.\n\nA gastroscope reveals evidence of significant gastritis but H.pylori testing is inconclusive. He is commenced on omeprazole and two antibiotics which improved his symptoms but on completing the course his symptoms returned a few days later. As such he was recommenced on the omeprazole long term.\n\nWhat adverse effect is the patient at risk of?",
