      "id": 165,
      "question": "A 54-year-old woman presents to the acute medical take with abnormal blood tests revealed by her GP.\n\nShe has a long history of fatigue, and is also feeling generally unwell with malaise and non-specific arthralgia. She has also been investigated by her GP for dry eyes and mouth, and a generalised itch.\n\nOn examination, she has excoriation marks over her arms, legs, and trunk. Otherwise she examines normally. Blood tests are shown below.\n\n\nHb\t135 g/L\tMale: (135-180)\nFemale: (115 - 160)\nBilirubin\t30 µmol/L\t(3 - 17)\nALP\t145 u/L\t(30 - 100)\nALT\t35 u/L\t(3 - 40)\nÎ³GT\t90 u/L\t(8 - 60)\nAlbumin\t45 g/L\t(35 - 50)\nAnti-mitochondrial antibodies\tPositive\n\nWhich of the following is the next most appropriate investigation?",
