      "question": "A 55-year-old inpatient with decompensated liver cirrhosis experiences high fever and reduced urine output. Investigations are performed including paracentesis of the peritoneal fluid which revealed a neutrophil count of 310 cells/µL indicating spontaneous bacterial peritonitis (SBP).\n\nCulture of the peritoneal fluid would most likely isolate which of the following organisms?",
