      "id": 180,
      "question": "A 49-year-old woman who is known to have alcoholic liver disease is admitted to the ward following a decompensation. A diagnosis of grade II hepatic encephalopathy is made. She is confused and a screen looking for infection and other precipitants is performed. She is started on lactulose. What other medication may be used to prevent the hepatic encephalopathy if lactulose is ineffective?",
