      "id": 187,
      "question": "A 64-year-old man presents to his GP with several months of dysphagia, weight loss and vomiting. He has a background of gastric oesophageal reflux disease (GORD) and is a smoker. The symptoms prompt the GP to urgently refer the patient to the hospital, where endoscopy is performed and a biopsy taken. This demonstrates an adenocarcinoma of the oesophagus.\n\nWhich of the following investigations should be performed next, to assess mural invasion?",
