      "id": 224,
      "question": "A 35-year-old former intravenous drug user is reviewed in the liver clinic. He has recently been diagnosed with hepatitis C after being found to have abnormal liver function tests. It is decided as part of his work-up that he should be assessed for liver cirrhosis. What is the most appropriate test to perform?",
