      "id": 244,
      "question": "A 52-year-old woman has 8 months of progressive fatigue, pruritus, and mild right upper quadrant discomfort. Her history includes Sjogren's syndrome, and she has never drunk alcohol or smoked.\n\nShe has mild scleral icterus, hepatomegaly, and skin excoriations. Her abdomen is otherwise non-distended and soft.\n\nInvestigations:\n\n\nBilirubin\t35 µmol/L\t(3 - 17)\nALP\t280 u/L\t(30 - 100)\nALT\t73 u/L\t(3 - 40)\nIgM\t4.5 g/L\t(0.4 - 2.5)\nAnti-nuclear antibodies\tpositive\nAnti-mitochondrial antibodies\tpositive\n\nWhich further test must be performed before a definitive diagnosis can be made?",
