      "question": "A 42-year-old man presents to the general surgical clinic for a routine follow-up appointment. He has a longstanding diagnosis of Crohn's disease and underwent an ileal resection 4 months ago. Since the operation, he has experienced ongoing diarrhoea. He denies any blood or weight loss. He has no fevers and feels otherwise well in himself.\n\nExamination and observations are all normal. Blood tests are performed:\n\n\nHb\t146 g/L\t(135-180)\nPlatelets\t256 * 109/L\t(150 - 400)\nWBC\t6.7 * 109/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\nNa+\t138 mmol/L\t(135 - 145)\nK+\t4.2 mmol/L\t(3.5 - 5.0)\nUrea\t6.2 mmol/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nCreatinine\t89 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\nCRP\t<5 mg/L\t(< 5)\n\nWhat is the most appropriate treatment?",
