      "id": 259,
      "question": "A 72-year-old woman is currently being assessed in the ward due to experiencing profuse diarrhoea. She has reported seven watery stool episodes in the last 24 hours, with no presence of blood. The patient has responded well to a five-day course of oral clarithromycin for pneumonia, which she is on the fourth day of completing. Physical examination reveals abdominal tenderness but no rigidity upon palpation.\n\n\n\tCurrent\tYesterday\nHb\t124 g/dL\t126 g/dL\nWCC\t15.3x10 9cells/L\t7.4 x10 9cells/L\nCRP\t123 mg/l\t98 mg/l\n\nWhat is the most appropriate infection control plan, considering the most likely diagnosis?",
