      "question": "A 36-year-old woman presents to the acute medical unit with sudden-onset severe upper abdominal pain and marked abdominal distension. She reports no previous liver disease but has recently noticed her legs swelling. Examination reveals tender hepatomegaly and ascites. Laboratory investigations show:\n\n\nALT\t132 IU/L\t(5–40)\nAlbumin\t28 g/L\t(35–50)\nBilirubin\t54 µmol/L\t(3–17)\nPlatelets\t410 * 109/L\t(150–400)\n\nShe is not pregnant and does not take any regular medication.\n\nWhat is the most likely underlying cause?",
