      "question": "A 65-year-old man presents to the clinic with a three-month history of fatigue, unintentional weight loss of 8 kg, and jaundice. He has dark urine and pale stools, without fever or significant abdominal pain. He smoked 30 cigarettes daily for the past 40 years but never used alcohol. No past medical history was noted apart from being diagnosed with diabetes recently.\n\nOn physical examination, icterus is noted. An abdominal ultrasound shows dilated biliary ducts without gallstones or liver masses.\n\n\nBilirubin\t42µmol/L\t(3 - 17)\nALP\t480 u/L\t(30 - 100)\nALT\t72 u/L\t(3 - 40)\nγGT\t220 u/L\t(8 - 60)\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
