      "question": "A 50-year-old man presents with recurrent flushing of the face and neck, accompanied by diarrhoea and abdominal cramping, for the past six months. He notes that these episodes occur predominantly after meals and during physical activity. The frequency and intensity of symptoms have been progressively worsening. Observations show a heart rate of 90 bpm, blood pressure 125/75 mmHg, temperature 37.2ºC, respiratory rate 20 breaths/min and oxygen saturation 96% on air.\n\nWhat is the most appropriate initial investigation?",
