      "question": "A 24-year-old man is referred to the colorectal outpatient clinic after a colonoscopy reveals more than 100 adenomatous polyps throughout his colon and rectum. He has no gastrointestinal symptoms but his father died of colorectal cancer at age 39. Genetic testing confirms an APC gene mutation. What is the most appropriate next step in management?",
