      "question": "A 25-year-old woman is referred by her GP to the gastroenterology clinic.\n\nShe has a background of type 1 diabetes mellitus and reports nine months of loose stools, abdominal cramps, and bloating. Her GP performed some initial investigations shown below.\n\n\nHb\t131 g/L\t(115 - 160)\nPlatelets\t265 * 109/L\t(150 - 400)\nWBC\t5.1 * 109/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\nCRP\t3 mg/L\t(< 5)\nStool culture\tNegative\nCoeliac screen\tNegative\nFaecal calprotectin\tNegative\n\nYou suspect she may have irritable bowel syndrome but given her diabetes you are also considering small bowel overgrowth syndrome.\n\nWhat is the most appropriate initial test in this case?",
