      "question": "A 21-year-old woman presents with diarrhoea and weight loss lasting several months. She has no significant past medical history except for depression and asthma. Physical examination reveals no obvious abnormalities and her blood tests are normal. She is referred for further investigations:\n\n\nColonoscopy\tDark-brown discolouration of the colon proximally. Samples taken.\nBiopsy\tLamina propria - pigment-laden macrophages.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
