      "question": "A 57-year-old male complains of painless abdominal distension over the past 2 months. He has a history of liver cirrhosis secondary to alcohol excess. He is otherwise well. Serum albumin ascites gradient (SAAG) is 15 (normal <11).\n\nWhat is the treatment of choice?",
