      "id": 384,
      "question": "A 62-year-old man presents to the emergency department with a three-month history of jaundice, weight loss, and dark urine. He reports generalised fatigue and a loss of appetite but denies experiencing significant abdominal pain.\n\nOn examination, scleral icterus is noted along with an epigastric mass.\n\nAn abdominal ultrasound reveals dilatation of both the common bile duct and the pancreatic duct, with no evidence of gallstones.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
