      "id": 3,
      "question": "A 23-year-old man presents with fever, sore throat, right-sided neck pain, and difficulty opening his mouth for five days. He now has a cough with purulent sputum and pleuritic chest pain. Examination shows tender neck swelling along the right sternocleidomastoid and unilateral peritonsillar swelling with uvular deviation. CT reveals internal jugular vein thrombosis and multiple cavitating lung nodules.\n\nWhat is the most likely causative organism?",
