      "question": "A 32-year-old male patient, with no significant past medical history, presented through the emergency department after recently returning from India, where he had undertaken a prolonged period of farming. He complained of continuous high-grade fevers for 9 days, bilateral subconjunctival haemorrhages with retro-orbital pain and severe myalgia.\n\nOn examination, there was maculopapular blanching erythema over the body which spared his palms and soles.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis here?",
