      "id": 39,
      "question": "A 27-year-old man presents with a 4-day history of fever, cough and malaise. He describes the cough as dry and also reports a headache. He has no significant past medical history and takes no regular medication.\n\nOn examination, he appears generally lethargic. Mild crackles are noted in the left lower lung field upon chest auscultation. A rash comprised of target lesions is noted across the torso and limbs. Observations are normal except for a temperature of 38.2ºC.\n\nWhat is the best diagnostic test for this patient?",
