      "question": "A 23-year-old woman attends a sexual health clinic with a 1-week history of increased vaginal discharge and mild lower abdominal discomfort. She reports unprotected vaginal sex with a man she met two months ago. Her last menstrual period was over six weeks ago.\n\nOn testing, she is confirmed to be pregnant and a first-pass urine NAAT confirms infection with Chlamydia trachomatis.\n\nWhat is the most appropriate treatment?",
