      "explanation": "Hepatitis C - 55-85% become chronically infected\n\nThe correct answer is\n\n55-85%\n\n. Hepatitis C virus (HCV) infection represents a major health issue worldwide. After acute infection with HCV, the majority of individuals are unable to clear the virus and develop chronic hepatitis, which can lead to cirrhosis and hepatocellular carcinoma. Studies have shown that 55-85% of individuals who contract HCV will develop chronic infection, depending on various factors including the individual's immune response and viral genotype."
