      "id": 54,
      "question": "A 34-year-old man presents to the infectious diseases clinic with a 2-week history of intermittent, bloody diarrhoea and mild abdominal pain. He returned from a 3-month work placement in rural India 6 weeks ago. He has not had any recent antibiotic use or contact with sick individuals. On examination, he is afebrile and his abdomen is soft with mild tenderness in the left iliac fossa. Laboratory investigations are as follows:\n\n\nHb\t13.6 g/dL\t(13.0 - 18.0)\nWBC\t7.1 ×109/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\nCRP\t6 mg/L\t(<5)\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
