      "id": 55,
      "question": "A 36-year-old man presents to his family physician complaining of swallowing difficulty. He reports that a few times he has been vomiting undigested food. He does not smoke or take alcohol. He has never had such symptoms in the past. He has no significant past medical or family history.\n\nHe works as a wildlife photographer and has repeatedly traveled to Argentina, Brazil, and Bolivia in the past. As far as he can remember he never had any serious infection while traveling except for the one time he had a swollen right eye which resolved now. A barium swallow revealed a bird's beak appearance of the esophagus.\n\nWhich of the following conditions does this patient most likely suffer from?",
