      "id": 71,
      "question": "A 23-year-old woman presents to a sexual health clinic. She had unprotected sexual intercourse with a man 3-4 weeks ago and has had six other sexual partners prior to this. The patient has no medical history and has never had a sexual-health screening.\n\nThe patient is currently asymptomatic but reports a flu-like illness one week ago which has since resolved.\n\nWhat is the most appropriate investigation?",
