      "question": "A 34-year-old farmer presents to the emergency department with a 3-day history of fevers and bloody diarrhoea. He is passing more than eight bowel motions a day. He reports that he regularly drinks unpasteurised milk.\n\nGiven the likely diagnosis, which treatment option is most appropriate?",
