      "id": 123,
      "question": "A 42-year-old man, who has newly-immigrated from Southeast Asia, presents with a number of complaints including abdominal pain and diarrhoea. He also has an intensely itchy rash which he thinks started on his buttocks but has since moved up his body rapidly. He believes that within the space of an hour the rash has spread 10 centimetres.\n\nExamination shows linear, urticarial streaks across the buttocks, which spreads up the back and across the abdomen. Blood tests show raised eosinophils. He is otherwise well, with no significant past medical history nor family history. He does not take any regular medications.\n\nGiven the likely diagnosis, what is the first-line treatment of choice?",
