      "id": 133,
      "question": "A 35-year-old man presents to the emergency department with a three-day history of fever, chills, and headache after recently returning from Nigeria. He is jaundiced and lethargic on examination. His vital signs are as follows:\n\n\nBlood pressure: 90/60 mmHg\nPulse: 110 bpm\nTemperature: 39.5°C\nRespiratory rate: 22/min\n\nInitial blood tests show:\n\n\nHb\t10.0 g/dL\t(13.8-17.2 g/dL)\nWBC\t12.5 x10 9/L\t(4.0-11.0 x10 9/L)\nPlatelets\t80 x10 9/L\t(150-450 x10 9/L)\nBilirubin\t45 µmol/L\t(3-17 µmol/L)\nALT\t45 U/L\t(10-40 U/L)\nAST\t50 U/L\t(10-40 U/L)\nCreatinine\t200 µmol/L\t(64-104 µmol/L)\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
