      "id": 149,
      "question": "A 45-year-old man attends the clinic with a flu-like illness. He has a one-week history of fever, sore throat, and a rash. On examination note a generalise maculopapular rash with sparing of the face. He describes unprotected anal sex with a male partner 3 weeks ago.\n\nWhat diagnostic test is recommended?",
