      "id": 166,
      "question": "A 36-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with skin lesions on her upper limbs. She has no past medical history or regular medications. However, she has recently been on extensive travels throughout the world. On examination, she has an annular granulomatous rash with an asymmetrical distribution, 3 lesions on her left arm, and 1 lesion on her right arm. The lesions are hypopigmented and have well defined raised borders. They are associated with hair loss and decreased sensation. She is systemically well and haemodynamically stable.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
