      "question": "A 31-year-old man has recently returned from a holiday in Brazil. For the past 3 days, he has been experiencing continuously high fevers and generalised aches and pains. He also reports a retro-orbital headache that worsens with eye movement. His appetite is generally reduced.\n\nOn examination, he has a temperature of 38.4ºC and a heart rate of 110 bpm. He appears generally unwell and his face is flushed. A widespread, blotchy rash is present. There is no abdominal tenderness, nor jaundice, nor organomegaly. Blood tests are as follows:\n\n\nHb\t138 g/L\tMale: (135-180)\nFemale: (115 - 160)\nPlatelets\t122 * 109/L\t(150 - 400)\nWBC\t3.8 * 109/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
