      "question": "A 33-year-old man presents to the emergency department with a 2-day history of nausea and headache. He describes a sensitivity to light and stiffness of the neck. The patient generally feels unwell and feverish.\n\nOn examination, he is pyrexial but other vital signs are within the normal range. He is not confused and no rashes are visible. There is objective neck stiffness but neurological examination is unremarkable. A lumbar puncture is performed and the result awaited.\n\nGiven the likely diagnosis, which of the following is the most likely cause?",
