      "question": "A 17-year-old female presents to the emergency department with a 2-day history of fevers, myalgia, and painful eyes. She has recently returned from a trip to the Democratic Republic of the Congo. She was not compliant with her anti-malarial medication during her trip due to gastrointestinal side effects. On examination, she has a temperature of 38.8ºC, she has clustered white lesions on her buccal mucosa and conjunctivitis.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
