      "question": "A 68-year-old man presents to the Emergency Department with a 2-day history of fever, productive cough, and right-sided pleuritic chest pain. He has a temperature of 39.2°C, respiratory rate of 24 breaths/minute, and oxygen saturation of 92% on room air. Examination reveals decreased breath sounds and crackles in the right lower zone. You notice cold sores on his lips. Chest X-ray shows right lower lobe consolidation.\n\nWhat is the most likely causative organism?",
