      "id": 201,
      "question": "A 24-year-old man presents with fever and abdominal pain. He returned from a holiday in Thailand one week ago.\n\nBlood results are as follows:\n\n\nHb\t115 g/L\tMale: (135-180)\nFemale: (115 - 160)\nPlatelets\t72 * 10 9/L\t(150 - 400)\nWBC\t20.2 * 10 9/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\nNa+\t135 mmol/L\t(135 - 145)\nK+\t4.8 mmol/L\t(3.5 - 5.0)\nUrea\t10.2 mmol/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nCreatinine\t105 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\nCRP\t182 mg/L\t(< 5)\n\nA rapid malaria antigen test, and blood films are requested'\n\n\nRapid malaria antigen test\tNegative\nThick and thin blood films\tEarly ring form trophozoites, late trophozoites and gametocytes present; Parasite count 2.5%\n\nWhat is the most likely cause?",
