      "id": 203,
      "question": "A 45-year-old man presents to the acute medical unit with diarrhoea. He has recently returned to the UK following a trip to rural Brazil. He notes that during this trip he had swum in local lakes, ate the local food and walked around the village without shoes. He remembers having a rash along the soles of his feet that was intensely itchy a week before returning to the UK.\n\nThe diarrhoea is intermittent and he recalls having type 7 stool over this time. There is also abdominal pains across the abdomen. There is no haematuria or dysuria associated. He remains systemically well with no other symptoms. The rash along the base of his feet has resolved.\n\nBlood tests results are as follow:\n\n\nHb\t140 g/L\tMale: (135-180)\nFemale: (115 - 160)\nPlatelets\t300 * 109/L\t(150 - 400)\nWBC\t10.0 * 109/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\nNeuts\t5.0 * 109/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nLymphs\t1.7 * 109/L\t(1.0 - 3.5)\nMono\t0.3 * 109/L\t(0.2 - 0.8)\nEosin\t3.0 * 109/L\t(0.0 - 0.4)\n\nStool samples were also taken and this was negative for Clostridium difficile. Microscopy results are awaited. A urine dip was performed and this did not show any blood, leukocytes or nitrites within the sample.\n\nWhat is the likely cause for his diarrhoea?",
