      "id": 209,
      "question": "A 25-year-old presents to the emergency department with a 3-day history of shortness of breath and fever. She has recently recovered from an influenza infection. She does not drink alcohol. There is no recent travel.\n\nObservations:\n\n\nHeart rate 111 beats per minute\nBlood pressure 100/55 mmHg\nRespiratory rate 24/minute\nOxygen saturation 92 % on room air\nTemperature 38.8 ºC\n\nOn examination, there are coarse crackles bilaterally.\n\nA chest-x-ray demonstrates bilateral consolidation with superimposed areas of lucency. Urinalysis is normal.\n\nWhat is the cause of this patient's presentation?",
