      "id": 221,
      "question": "A 29-year-old man is admitted to the infectious diseases unit with several days of fever, rigors and headache. He has just returned from an extended trip to rural Thailand and admits to non-adherence to his malaria prophylaxis. He has no significant past medical history.\n\nOn examination, he appears generally unwell and splenomegaly is palpable. Over several days of monitoring, he is noted to have a cyclical fever, with his temperature spiking every 24 hours.\n\nWhat is the most likely species that he has been infected with?",
