      "id": 238,
      "question": "A 43-year-old man presents to the infectious disease unit with a 4-week history of fever and lethargy. He has noticed pale bumps associated with a severely red and itchy rash around both his ankles. He reports bloating and myalgia. He has recently returned from a trip to Egypt and reports taking anti-malarials. Observations reveal a temperature of 38.1 ºC. On examination, he has an enlarged spleen. Chest X-ray reveals bilateral infiltrates. Blood tests show raised inflammatory markers with marked eosinophilia.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
