      "id": 258,
      "question": "A 40-year-old man originally from Cambodia is referred to the infectious disease clinic having presented with non-specific respiratory symptoms including a dry cough, shortness of breath and burning of the chest and chronic diarrhoea.\n\nBlood tests identify eosinophilia, and a chest x-ray shows pulmonary infiltrates. Also, stool sample microscopy reveals the presence of small rhabditiform larvae.\n\nWhat medication is first-line in this patient's condition?",
