      "question": "A 62-year-old man presents to the emergency department following an injury gardening, in which he cut his hand. He is experiencing intermittent tonic contractions of the skeletal muscles which are intensely painful, during which he remains conscious. On examination, he has evident trismus and opisthotonus.\n\nWhat is the mechanism of action of the toxin in this condition?",
