      "question": "A 26-year-old man attends the infectious disease clinic. He has returned from 4 months of travelling in rural Southeast Asia two weeks previously. Over the last few days, he has become unwell with fevers and headaches. There is a non-blanching maculopapular rash over his arms and legs, which he states started on his trunk, sparing the soles of his feet and the palms of his hands. There are no ulcers.\n\nThere is no history of any insect bites, but he did stay in several hostels with vermin. He was not sexually active whilst travelling.\n\nWhat would be the appropriate treatment for this patient?",
