      "id": 263,
      "question": "A 55-year-old man is referred to the medical admissions unit. He recently returned from a holiday in Italy and has failed to respond to a course of co-amoxiclav for a suspected lower respiratory tract infection. Chest x-ray shows bilateral infiltrates. Bloods are as follows:\n\n\nNa+\t122 mmol/l\nK+\t4.3 mmol/l\nUrea\t8.4 mmol/l\nCreatinine\t130 µmol/l\n\nWhat is the likely diagnosis?",
