      "explanation": "The most common causes of viral meningitis in adults are enteroviruses\n\nThis patient has viral meningitis. This is the most likely diagnosis because of the CSF findings of clear fluid, high protein, normal/high glucose and the presence of 50-1000 cells/µL, mainly lymphocytes.\n\nEnteroviruses\n\nare the most common cause of viral meningitis in adults.\n\nHIV\n\nand\n\nCMV\n\nare also causes of viral meningitis in adults but are less common. CMV meningitis mostly occurs in immunocompromised patients, such as organ transplant recipients.\n\nThe other options on the list are bacterial causes of meningitis. CSF in bacterial meningitis, by contrast, is turbid/cloudy in colour, has low glucose and a neutrophil-predominant cellular component. As such the answer is not\n\nNeisseria meningitidis\n\nor\n\nStreptococcus pneumoniae\n\n, although these are both common causes of bacterial meningitis in adults."
