      "question": "A 27-year-old woman presents with a headache and a tremor affecting her right arm. She has just returned from a trip visiting family in rural India.\n\nOn examination, there is a fever of 38.5 degrees Celsius and multiple mosquito bites on the arms. On neurological examination, the cranial nerves are all intact. There is increased tone on the right with cogwheel rigidity in the right upper limb, and a 5Hz tremor affecting her right arm. Her power, reflexes and sensation are all normal.\n\nWhat area of the brain is most likely to be inflamed in this patient?",
