      "id": 295,
      "question": "A 39-year-old Greek farmer presents to you with a skin lesion on his shin. It began yesterday morning as a small pruritic blister but has developed into a black ulcer. On examination, the lesion is approximately 3cm² and has a central area of necrotic tissue. The ulcer is non-tender and there is notable oedema surrounding the ulcer. He is otherwise well in himself.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
