      "id": 296,
      "question": "A 50-year-old man presents to the emergency department with fevers, poor appetite and weight loss after returning from Brazil 4 weeks ago. He is normally fit and well.\n\nOn examination, he has a fever of 39.4ºC but observations are otherwise normal. He has a grey discolouration of his skin. He has a palpably enlarged spleen and liver.\n\nBloods are performed.\n\n\nHb\t67 g/L\tMale: (135-180)\nFemale: (115 - 160)\nPlatelets\t102 * 10 9/L\t(150 - 400)\nWBC\t2.4 * 10 9/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\nCreatinine\t346 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\n\nAn urgent bone marrow biopsy is arranged.\n\nWhat treatment will likely be first line?",
