      "question": "A 25-year-old female patient presents to the emergency department with a 2-day history of bloody diarrhoea and abdominal pain. She was admitted under the medical team for intravenous rehydration therapy. The next day, she developed general oedema with sudden drop in her urine output. An urgent blood sample was sent with the results below.\n\n\nHb\t9.0 g/dL\nUrea\t30.3 mmol/L\nCreatinine\t285µmol/L\nPeripheral blood film\tpresence of schistocytes\n\nWhat is the likely infection causing this clinical picture?",
