      "correctText": "Cholera",
      "explanation": "E.coli O157: H7 is the strain causing haemolytic uraemic syndrome\n\nThe clinical picture suggests the haemolytic uraemic syndrome. The patient has a combination of bloody diarrhoea, acute renal failure with a high urea and haemolytic anaemia (as confirmed by the presence of schistocytes). E.coli O157: H7 is the strain causing haemolytic uraemic syndrome.\n\nSalmonella, shigella and campylobacter can cause bloody diarrhoea but do not commonly cause haemolytic anaemia.\n\nCholera is not a cause of bloody diarrhoea."
