      "correctIndex": 0,
      "correctText": "Ciprofloxacin",
      "explanation": "Ciprofloxacin promotes acquisition of MRSA\n\nThe correct answer is\n\nciprofloxacin\n\n. This quinolone antibiotic has good efficacy against gram-negative organisms including\n\nPseudomonas aeruginosa\n\n. Its use is well-recognised to promote the acquisition of MRSA. All the other answers listed here can be used to treat MRSA infections.\n\nClindamycin\n\nis incorrect. Clindamycin is a broad-spectrum antibiotic belonging to the class of lincosamides. It can be used to treat gram-positive and anaerobic infections. Rather than promoting the acquisition of MRSA, it can be used to treat this organism.\n\nGentamicin\n\nis incorrect. As an aminoglycoside, gentamicin primarily acts against gram-negative organisms. It also has some activity against MRSA, but should not generally be used as monotherapy. It has more of a role in synergistic therapy.\n\nLinezolid\n\nis incorrect. This belongs to the class of oxazolidinones. It has very high bioavailability and is effective against gram-positive organisms, including MRSA.\n\nRifampicin\n\nis incorrect. It has some activity against MRSA but should not be used alone as resistance develops easily. It can be used in combination therapy against infections involving biofilm, such as in prosthetic joint infections."
