      "question": "A 32-year-old presents with a two-month history of fever, weight loss, fatigue, and abdominal discomfort. He recently returned from South Sudan, where he was volunteering in a rural area.\n\nOn examination, he appears pale, with significant hepatosplenomegaly. There are no rashes or visible skin lesions.\n\nInvestigations reveal:\n\nTest\tResult\tNormal range\nHaemoglobin\t85 g/L\t135–175\nWhite cell count\t2.5 × 10⁹/L\t4–11\nPlatelets\t75 × 10⁹/L\t150–400\nCRP\t20 mg/L\t< 10\nALT\t35 IU/L\t10–40\nAlbumin\t30 g/L\t35–50\n\nA bone marrow aspirate reveals macrophages containing amastigotes.\n\nWhat is the most appropriate management for this patient?",
