      "question": "A 19-year-old man presents 3 days after returning from a backpacking trip across Brazil. He complains of a sudden onset fever, headache, joint pains and rash all over his body. He has no existing health conditions and is not on any medication.\n\nOn examination he has a petechial rash on his limbs. He has no focal neurology and no signs of meningism.\n\n\nHb\t100 g/l\nPlatelets\t80 * 109/l\nWBC\t4.0 * 109/l\nEosinophils\t0.4 * 109/l\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
