      "question": "A 25-year-old woman presents with a 48-hour history of worsening headache and fever. On examination, you note nuchal rigidity and photophobia. A neurological examination is normal.\n\nBlood results are as follows:\n\n\nHb\t115 g/L\tMale: (135-180)\nFemale: (115 - 160)\nPlatelets\t248 * 109/L\t(150 - 400)\nWBC\t8.2 * 109/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\nNa+\t136 mmol/L\t(135 - 145)\nK+\t4.6 mmol/L\t(3.5 - 5.0)\nUrea\t4.4 mmol/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nCreatinine\t58 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\nCRP\t48 mg/L\t(< 5)\nGlucose\t6.8 mmol/L\t(4-7)\n\nA lumbar puncture is performed:\n\n\nOpening pressure\t14 cm H2O\t(7-18)\nWBC count\t125 cells/µL (90% lymphocytes)\t(0-5)\nGlucose\t5.4 mmol/L\t(> 0.7 x serum glucose)\nProtein\t82 mg/dL\t(<45)\n\nWhat is the most likely pathogen?",
