      "question": "A 34-year-old woman with rheumatoid arthritis, currently taking methotrexate and prednisolone, is admitted to the rheumatology ward for management of a disease flare. On day 2 of her admission, she shares a bay with another patient who develops a vesicular rash later confirmed as chickenpox. She has no history of previous chickenpox or vaccination. Her bloods are as follows:\n\n\nVaricella-zoster IgG antibody titre\t<80 mIU/mL\tImmunosuppressed: (<150 indicates susceptibility)\n\nWhat is the most appropriate next step in her management?",
