      "id": 428,
      "question": "A 54 year old female is admitted with a severe pneumonia following a holiday in Turkey. Bloods reveal both hyponatraemia and deranged liver function tests. A chest x-ray shows patchy alveolar infiltrates with consolidation in the right lower lobe. Which one of the following investigations is most likely to confirm the probable diagnosis?",
