      "explanation": "Oral ciprofloxacin or rifampicin is used as prophylaxis for contacts of patients with meningococcal meningitis\n\nOral\n\nciprofloxacin\n\nis used as prophylaxis for contacts of patients with meningococcal meningitis. Rifampicin is also used but is not on the list of options.\n\nCeftriaxone\n\nis an empirical treatment for adults with suspected meningitis. Given the parents are well with no signs or symptoms of meningitis, this treatment is not indicated.\n\nAmoxicillin\n\nis given in addition to ceftriaxone for certain vulnerable patients who are more likely to have contracted gram-positive infections (<3 months old; >60 years old; immunocompromised). Again, this is not relevant for the parents given they are currently well.\n\nDoxycycline\n\nis used to treat syphilitic meningitis, a type of neurosyphilis. Given the confirmed presence of\n\nNeisseria meningitidis\n\non CSF analysis, it is not indicated in this case.\n\nContacts of patients with meningococcal meningitis are recommended to take prophylactic antibiotics\n\neven if asymptomatic\n\n. Contacts of patients with pneumococcal meningitis generally are not offered prophylactic antibiotics."
