      "explanation": "Anthrax presents with a black eschar that is typically painless; it is treated with ciprofloxacin\n\nIntravenous drug use may cause acute skin infection, often caused by Streptococcal or Staphylococcal species (both gram-positive cocci). Rarely, heroin may be contaminated with\n\nBacillus anthracis\n\nor\n\nClostridia\n\nspecies, including\n\nC. botulinum\n\n,\n\nC. perfringens\n\nand\n\nC. novyi\n\n.\n\nBacillus anthracis\n\n(anthrax) is a spore-forming, aerobic gram-positive bacillus.\n\nClostridia\n\nspecies are also spore-forming gram-positive bacilli but they are anaerobic. Cutaneous anthrax may present with a black eschar lesion (differentials for this include Rickettsia). In a review of UK cases of anthrax associated with intravenous drug use, eschar was not always present. Although treatment would be based on sensitivities, cutaneous anthrax is typically treated with ciprofloxacin or doxycycline.\n\nClindamycin is useful for Staphylococcal bone and joint infections such as osteomyelitis, including methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA).\n\nDaptomycin may be used for complicated skin and soft-tissue infections caused by gram-positive bacteria, including MRSA. Like vancomycin, it does act against gram-negative bacteria. Due to its activity against gram-positive bacteria, it may be an alternative antibiotic depending on sensitivities but it is not the first-line choice in the treatment of anthrax.\n\nFlucloxacillin is useful against Infections due to beta-lactamase-producing staphylococci. It has a role in the treatment of skin infections including impetigo, cellulitis, erysipelas, diabetic foot infections, infected leg ulcers and osteomyelitis. It is not the first-line choice in the treatment of anthrax.\n\nVancomycin may also be used for complicated skin and soft-tissue infections caused by gram-positive bacteria, including MRSA. It does not act against gram-negative bacteria. Due to its activity against gram-positive bacteria, it may be an alternative antibiotic depending on sensitivities but it is not the first-line choice in the treatment of anthrax."
