      "explanation": "E. coli\n\nEscherichia coli\n\nis correct. This patient is experiencing traveller's diarrhoea. The most common cause of this is\n\nEscherichia coli\n\n.\n\nSalmonella typhi\n\nis incorrect. This is the organism responsible for typhoid fever. This patient does not have typhoid fever; this would be characterised by a high fever accompanied by abdominal pain, constipation and vomiting. Diarrhoea is unusual.\n\nShigella\n\nis incorrect.\n\nShigella\n\nproduces prolonged, bloody diarrhoea and fevers.\n\nStaphylococcus aureus\n\nis incorrect. This produces severe vomiting, followed by watery diarrhoea. Vomiting is not a feature in this patient, so this answer is incorrect.\n\nVibrio cholerae\n\nis incorrect. This is the organism that produces cholera. Cholera is characterised by severe watery diarrhoea resulting in dehydration and systemic upset. This is not described in this case, making\n\nVibrio cholerae\n\nincorrect."
