      "id": 476,
      "question": "A 44-year-old woman attends with a one-week history of a productive cough and shortness of breath. She recently was diagnosed with influenza A. She keeps a parrot as a pet. Observations are as follows: heart rate 115 beats per minute, blood pressure 135/80 mmHg, temperature 38.6ºC, respiratory rate 20 breaths per minute, and oxygen saturation 92% on air.\n\nA chest x-ray was performed:\n\n\nChest x-ray\tRight-sided lobar pneumonia with evidence of cavitation\n\nWhat organism is most likely implicated?",
