      "explanation": "Human bites, like animal bites, should be treated with co-amoxiclav\n\nCo-amoxiclav would adequately cover the main organisms implicated in a human bite. This includes\n\nStreptococcus\n\n,\n\nStaphylococcus\n\n,\n\nEikenella\n\n,\n\nCorynebacterium\n\nand other anaerobes. Even if there are no signs of infection antibiotics should be prescribed.\n\nMetronidazole with clarithromycin (or doxycycline) can be used and is generally reserved for patients who are penicillin-allergic. This should also be avoided in this particular patient as a disulfiram-like reaction may occur due to his intoxication.\n\nDoxycycline alone can be used if other medications are not available but will not be as effective.\n\nAmoxicillin would not cover the β-lactamase producing bacteria."
