      "question": "A 52-year-old man attends with a 48-hour history of productive cough. He works as a dairy farmer. You note a cold sore on his lower lip, Observations are as follows: heart rate 105 beats per minute, blood pressure 125/75 mmHg, temperature 38.2ºC, respiratory rate 18 breaths per minute, oxygen saturation 95% on air.\n\nBlood results are as follows:\n\n\nHb\t115 g/L\tMale: (135-180)\nFemale: (115 - 160)\nPlatelets\t168 * 109/L\t(150 - 400)\nWBC\t20.4 * 109/L\t(4.0 - 11.0)\nNa+\t138 mmol/L\t(135 - 145)\nK+\t4.2 mmol/L\t(3.5 - 5.0)\nUrea\t6.1 mmol/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nCreatinine\t72 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\nCRP\t224 mg/L\t(< 5)\n\nA chest x-ray was performed:\n\n\nChest x-ray\tLeft-sided lobar pneumonia\n\nWhat organism is most likely implicated?",
