      "id": 43,
      "question": "A 32-year-old man has been referred to the clinic due to a two-month history of loin pain and haematuria. He mentions that his family has a history of an inherited condition primarily impacting the kidneys. Several years ago, he was advised to undergo screening tests, but he chose not to.\n\nOn examination, the patient exhibits bilaterally palpable masses. A renal ultrasound scan reveals the presence of over 10 cysts in both kidneys.\n\nWhat other complication is most associated with the patient's likely diagnosis?",
