      "id": 46,
      "question": "A 35-year-old man is receiving dialysis following a childhood diagnosis of an inherited condition. He initially presented with microscopic haematuria, progressive renal failure and bilateral sensorineural deafness. He was diagnosed following genetic testing and a renal biopsy which showed longitudinal splitting of the lamina densa of the glomerular basement membrane with a 'basket-weave' appearance.\n\nHow is the underlying condition inherited in the majority of cases?",
