      "id": 66,
      "question": "An 81-year-old woman with chronic kidney disease and diabetes mellitus presented with progressive leg pain associated with painful skin ulcers. There were severely painful, firm, indurated plaques on the lower extremities. The plaques recently progressed to involve larger areas with associated local ulceration and necrosis.\n\nPhysical examination demonstrated peripheral oedema and severely painful necrotic skin ulcers 3Ã—6 cm in diameter on the medial side of proximal lower limbs bilaterally, with black eschar and surrounding erythema.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis in this case?",
