      "question": "A 46-year-old, with an end-stage chronic kidney disease secondary to diabetes, undertakes a renal transplantation with no immediate complications. Two months later, he attends the emergency department with a 3-day history of a febrile syndrome and right upper quadrant pain. Investigations showed a moderated leukopenia and mild transaminasaemia.\n\n\nHb\t119 g/l\nPlatelets\t234 * 109/l\nWBC\t2.46 * 109/l\n\n\nALP\t61 u/l\nALT\t75 u/l\nγGT\t72 u/l\nAlbumin\t38 g/l\n\nWhat would be your first diagnostic impression?",
