      "id": 98,
      "question": "A 22-year-old man is referred with a 3-month history of progressive ankle swelling and facial puffiness. He has also noticed frothy urine but denies haematuria or systemic symptoms.\n\nOn examination, he has bilateral pitting oedema to the mid-shin and a blood pressure of 148/92 mmHg.\n\n\n\nNa\t139 mmol/L\t(135–145)\nK\t4.1 mmol/L\t(3.5–5.0)\nUr\t6.5 mmol/L\t(2.5–7.8)\nCr\t103 µmol/L\t(60–110)\nComplement C3\t0.55 g/L\t(0.75–1.65)\nComplement C4\t0.26 g/L\t(0.14–0.54)\nUrinalysis\tProtein +++ ; Blood ++\n\nA renal biopsy reveals dense intramembranous electron-dense deposits on electron microscopy.\n\nWhat is commonly associated with the type 2 variant of the most likely diagnosis?",
