      "question": "A 36-year-old man presents to the emergency department with right flank pain radiating from loin to groin. He reports no past medical history and consumes 25 units of alcohol per week.\n\nOn examination, he appears extremely restless and has experienced vomiting due to the pain, which is relieved by diclofenac administered rectally.\n\nThe following investigations have been arranged:\n\n\n24 hour urinary calcium\t723 mg\t(100-300)\nSerum urate\t320 mmol/L\t(< 420)\n\nWhat treatment can reduce the risk of this problem recurring?",
