      "id": 102,
      "question": "A 42-year-old man with known HIV presents with swelling of his lower limbs, shortness of breath and frothy urine. He has been lost to follow-up and admits he has not taken his anti-retroviral medications for several years.\n\nOn examination, he has clear evidence of fluid overload and a urine dip confirms the presence of a large amount of protein.\n\nWhat form of nephropathy is most likely to be found in this patient?",
