      "id": 122,
      "question": "A 27-year-old woman presents with facial and bilateral leg swelling in the context of a recent viral upper respiratory tract infection.\n\nThe patient takes no regular or over-the-counter medications.\n\nExamination reveals facial, sacral and peripheral pitting oedema.\n\n\nNa+\t137 mmol/L\t(135 - 145)\nK+\t4.8 mmol/L\t(3.5 - 5.0)\nUrea\t6.3 mmol/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nCreatinine\t167 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\nAlbumin\t13 g/L\t(35 - 55)\n\n\nUrine Protein:Creatinine Ratio\t755 mg/mmol\t(< 15)\n\nA kidney biopsy shows normal appearances on light microscopy and no immune complex deposition on immunofluorescence. Electron microscopy is awaited.\n\nWhat is the definitive treatment for the likely underlying condition?",
