      "question": "A 36-year-old man is admitted to the acute medical unit with confusion and dehydration. He reports drinking heavily at a party the previous evening, after which he developed frequent urination and intense thirst. He has no past medical history and takes no regular medications. His vital signs are stable. Laboratory results are as follows:\n\n\nNa+\t148 mmol/L\t(135 - 145)\nK+\t4.2 mmol/L\t(3.5 - 5.0)\nGlucose\t5.8 mmol/L\t(3.9 - 6.1)\nUrea\t6.1 mmol/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nCreatinine\t80 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\n\nWhat is the most likely mechanism for his symptoms?",
