      "id": 180,
      "question": "A 19-year-old man presents to the nephrology clinic with a history of persistent microscopic haematuria and progressive hearing loss since childhood. He has recently developed worsening fatigue. His maternal uncle required dialysis in his twenties. Urinalysis reveals proteinuria. Renal biopsy electron microscopy shows splitting of the glomerular basement membrane lamina densa. Which genetic inheritance pattern is most likely responsible for his condition?",
