      "question": "A 55-year-old female presents with polyuria and polydipsia, which has been on-going for 11 weeks. She has hypertension and bipolar disorder and is currently taking amlodipine and lithium.\n\nA water deprivation test is carried out:\n\n\nPre-test urine osmolality 250 mOsm/kg\t(500-850)\nPost-test urine osmolality 274 mOsm/kg\t(500-850)\n\nWhat is the pathogenesis of the likely diagnosis?",
