      "id": 208,
      "question": "A 14-year-old girl is referred to the paediatric unit with reduced urine output and lethargy. She has been passing bloody diarrhoea for the past four days. On admission she appears dehydrated. Bloods show the following:\n\n\nNa+\t142 mmol/l\nK+\t4.8 mmol/l\nBicarbonate\t22 mmol/l\nUrea\t10.1 mmol/l\nCreatinine\t176 µmol/l\n\n\nHb\t10.4 g/dl\nMCV\t90 fl\nPlt\t91 * 109/l\nWBC\t14.4 * 109/l\n\nGiven the likely diagnosis, which one of the following organisms is the most likely cause?",
