      "question": "A 25-year-old woman with a history of end-stage renal disease secondary to focal segmental glomerulosclerosis presents to the Emergency Department. For the past 12 months she has used Continuous Ambulatory Peritoneal Dialysis (CAPD). She feels generally unwell with abdominal pain and a fever. She also describes her last bag as being 'cloudy'. Which organism is most likely to be responsible for this presentation?",
