      "question": "A 55-year-old male is being evaluated for persistent proteinuria. He has a past medical history of multiple myeloma that has recently relapsed. He undergoes renal biopsy. Light microscopy with Congo red stain reveals apple-green birefringence under polarised light.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
