      "id": 224,
      "question": "A 78-year-old man presents with shortness of breath. A chest x-ray demonstrates pulmonary oedema. He was recently started on an ACE inhibitor for hypertension.\n\nBlood results are as follows:\n\n\nNa+\t135 mmol/L\t(135 - 145)\nK+\t4.2 mmol/L\t(3.5 - 5.0)\nBicarbonate\t20 mmol/L\t(22 - 29)\nUrea\t14.6 mmol/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nCreatinine\t196 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\n\nBlood results from the clinic 2 weeks ago prior to starting an ACE inhibitor are as follows:\n\n\nNa+\t138 mmol/L\t(135 - 145)\nK+\t3.6 mmol/L\t(3.5 - 5.0)\nBicarbonate\t24 mmol/L\t(22 - 29)\nUrea\t7.2 mmol/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nCreatinine\t110 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\n\nWhat investigation should be arranged?",
