      "question": "A 56-year-old man presents to the urology clinic. He has suffered from recurrent episodes of renal colic. CT scans have shown multiple stones and 24-hour urine collection reveals high urinary calcium.\n\nWhat is the single best medication that might reduce his stone formation?",
