      "id": 248,
      "question": "A 34-year-old man is being reviewed in the renal clinic following a diagnosis of autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease (ADPKD). He initially presented with haematuria and was diagnosed after an ultrasound scan. He has no knowledge of his family history as he was adopted.\n\nCurrently, his renal function is stable, but he is concerned about potential complications that may arise from his condition.\n\nWhat complication is most likely to develop in this patient?",
