      "question": "A 52-year-old with a history of arthritis, previous gastric ulcers, diabetic and hypertension has been vomiting and having diarrhoea for the last 12 hours. He takes naproxen, misoprostol, levothyroxine, linagliptin and long-acting insulin. With regards to glomerular filtration, which of the following can reduce glomerular filtration and contribute to development of an acute kidney injury?",
