      "question": "A 58-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with haematuria and oliguria. She has a history of sinusitis over the past few months with associated haemorrhagic discharge. Examination reveals hypertension and urinalysis demonstrates proteinuria and haematuria. Blood tests are performed, with the results below:\n\n\nNa+\t136 mmol/L\t(135 - 145)\nK+\t5.6 mmol/L\t(3.5 - 5.0)\nUrea\t22.1 mmol/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nCreatinine\t376 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\ncANCA\tPositive\n\nThe patient is referred to the renal team who performs a biopsy as part of their workup.\n\nWhich of the following biopsy findings is most likely?",
