      "explanation": "Absence seizures - good prognosis: 90-95% become seizure free in adolescence\n\n90-95% is the correct answer. A history of multiple, short seizures that are quick to resolve is indicative of absence seizures. In children, these can be precipitated by times of stress and hyperventilation and are usually describes as a vacant episode with the patient staring blankly. Absence seizures have a good prognosis and 90-95% of children will become seizure-free in adolescence."
