      "id": 69,
      "question": "A 64-year-old woman presents with migraine and her daughter says that she noticed that when she asked her mum to repeat a phrase she said she could not.\n\nThe patient has been having migraines for years and they have always been accompanied by a visual aura of flashing lights and nil else. There are no focal neurological signs and CT brain is unremarkable.\n\nUpon further questioning, the patient can follow simple and complex commands (open eyes and touch left hand to right ear) and when asked can name 4 animals in a minute. She is also fluent and understandable when asking her general questions. However, when the patient is asked to repeat 3 simple words and a sentence she cannot.\n\nWhat is this type of dysphasia?",
