      "question": "A 26-year-old Asian woman with no medical background presented with altered mental state, headaches, and seizures. She had a dermal filler injection of her lip for aesthetic purposes performed 1-month prior to her acute presentation. Upon clinical review, she underwent imaging of her brain with an initial CT scan. The scan revealed the presence of tenuous low-density changes within regions of the anterior and medial temporal lobe as well as the island of Reil.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis in this case?",
