      "id": 136,
      "question": "A 38-year-old woman is seen in the neurology clinic with a four-week history of progressive neurological symptoms. She has a diagnosis of relapsing-remitting multiple sclerosis and has been receiving her initial disease-modifying therapy for approximately 3 years.\n\nNeurological examination reveals truncal and limb ataxia, as well as weakness in her right arm and leg.\n\nA brain MRI reveals hyperintense lesions on T2-weighted images.\n\nSerological testing identifies antibodies to the JC virus.\n\nWhat medication is most likely to be responsible for this clinical presentation?",
