      "explanation": "Lip smacking + post-ictal dysphasia are localising features of a temporal lobe seizure\n\nThe temporal lobe is correct. The combination of a recurrent sense of dejÃ  vu associated with episodes of lip-smacking and postictal dysphasia suggest a temporal lobe seizure.\n\nThe frontal lobe is incorrect. Partial seizures affecting the frontal lobe give rise to predominantly motor symptoms e.g. head/leg movements, posturing, post-ictal weakness or a Jacksonian march.\n\nThe occipital lobe is incorrect. Seizures affecting this part of the brain typically cause visual symptoms such as floaters/flashes.\n\nThe parietal lobe is incorrect. Seizures in this region tend to be associated with paraesthesia.\n\nWhole-brain is incorrect. Seizures affecting the whole brain are by definition generalized and would therefore cause a loss of consciousness and a generalized tonic-clonic seizure."
