      "correctText": "CT kidney, ureters, and bladder",
      "explanation": "Multiple sclerosis patient with bladder dysfunction - get an ultrasound first to assess bladder emptying\n\nThis patient has recurrent urinary tract infections likely due to urinary retention secondary to multiple sclerosis (MS). A post-micturition bladder scan is a first-line investigation to assess bladder emptying in patients with MS.\n\nA CT kidneys ureters bladder would not be an adequate first-line investigation for bladder dysfunction and would expose a young woman to unnecessary radiation.\n\nFlow cytometry is not a first-line indication for bladder dysfunction in MS.\n\nUS bladder would assess the patient's bladder emptying and residual volume if done following micturition and would help diagnose bladder dysfunction in MS. It is the first-line investigation.\n\nA vaginal swab is not indicated given that she has one sexual partner and has no symptoms of sexually transmitted infections.\n\nMRI brain to investigate for new brain lesions in multiple sclerosis is not indicated in this acute setting of urinary retention. Note that there is no evidence of new symptoms or new central nervous system lesions."
