      "id": 381,
      "question": "A 19-year-old woman is referred to the neurology outpatient department with 2 years of progressive weakness. She notices that she finds it difficult to walk upstairs and lift heavy objects over her head. Her mother has commented that her smile doesn't seem quite as 'bright' as it was previously. She has no significant past medical history and is not on any regular medications. She does not smoke or drink alcohol.\n\nOn examination, she has difficulty closing her eyes and smiling. Power is 4+/5 at the proximal muscles of the upper and lower limbs. There is no rash.\n\nWhat is the likely diagnosis?",
