      "question": "A 32-year-old nursery teacher complains of progressive hearing loss and tinnitus over the past three months. She denies aural fullness and recent infections. The patient recalls that her mother was diagnosed with a 'hearing problem' in her thirties.\n\nExternal examination of the ear is normal. Rinne test: bone conduction is louder than air conduction in both ears. Weber test: sound localised to the centre of the forehead.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
