      "id": 426,
      "question": "A 16-year-old girl is seen in the clinic with suspected complex partial seizures following several episodes of impaired consciousness and automatic features including lip-smacking and chewing. Further investigation confirms the likely diagnosis, and the child is started on a medication for the condition.\n\nA few days later however the child is rushed into hospital with a several, global rash with blistering and peeling of the skin. The mucous membranes are also involved and there is evidence of end-organ failure.\n\nWhat medication was the child most likely started on?",
