      "question": "A 13-year-old child with a diagnosis of tuberous sclerosis presents to the clinic with his mother. She explains how her son has had two episodes of haematuria and bouts of flank pain with nausea and vomiting. Multiple investigations are performed including an MRI scan which reveals a kidney abnormality.\n\nWhich of the following is the most likely cause of the symptoms?",
