      "id": 46,
      "question": "A 41-year-old woman with a history of type 1 diabetes attends a routine eye screening appointment. She is found to have retinal neovascularisation, fibrous tissue anterior to the retinal disc.\n\nShe is advised she will require treatment and counselled that following this treatment up to 50% of patients have a noticeable reduction in their visual field.\n\nWhat treatment will she be offered?",
