      "question": "A 66-year-old man presents to his GP complaining of 'funny symptoms' in his eyes. He describes having flashes of light in his eyes for several days. In addition to this, he has been noticing darker 'bits' floating around in his vision. He denies any pain. He is short-sighted and wears glasses but otherwise has no significant past medical history.\n\nOn examination, the visual acuity and fields are normal.\n\nWhat is the most likely cause of his symptoms?",
