      "question": "A 74-year-old man presents to the emergency department with sudden, painless loss of vision in his right eye. He denies headache, photophobia, flashers/floaters or painful eye movements. He has a past medical history of hypertension and ischaemic heart disease.\n\nOn examination, the acuity in the right eye is reduced to finger counting. The acuity in the left eye is normal. On fundoscopy, retinal haemorrhages are evident. Eye movements are normal in all directions. The red reflex is present.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
