      "question": "You are asked to review a patient on the palliative ward who was recently diagnosed with end-stage pancreatic cancer. Due to the poor prognosis, they were started on a standard dose of 20mg of modified released morphine, twice a day with additional morphine for breakthrough pain.\n\nOn discussion with the patient, they report that they are still experiencing severe abdominal pain but was unaware they could request further analgesia and therefore have not had any breakthrough morphine.\n\nThe patient has no other comorbidities and is not on any other medications.\n\nGiven the patient is still experiencing pain what adjustment should you make to their morphine dose?",
