      "question": "A 63-year-old patient presents to the emergency department with reports of haematemesis and black stools. She has a background of alcohol excess and typically drinks 8 units per day.\n\nYou initiate basic management and start seeing another patient when a crash call sounds, and you find the patient having a seizure.\n\nWhat is the most likely time period since she last consumed alcohol?",
