      "id": 53,
      "question": "A 35-year-old woman visits the emergency department complaining of fatigue and headaches. She mentions experiencing irregular menstrual cycles for the past three months. Her past medical history includes bipolar disorder, for which she started taking aripiprazole four months ago.\n\nThe following blood tests were conducted:\n\n\nNa+\t141 mmol/L\t(135 - 145)\nK+\t4.2 mmol/L\t(3.5 - 5.0)\nBicarbonate\t26 mmol/L\t(22 - 29)\nUrea\t4.5 mmol/L\t(2.0 - 7.0)\nCreatinine\t102 µmol/L\t(55 - 120)\n\n\nThyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH)\t7.3 mU/L\t(0.5-5.5)\nFree thyroxine (T4)\t11.2 pmol/L\t(9.0 - 18)\n\n\nProlactin\t2234 ng/mL\t(< 20)\n\nWhat is the most likely cause of this woman's abnormal blood results?",
