      "question": "A 54-year-old man is brought to his general practitioner by his wife. She is concerned that he is not eating or drinking. He has a past medical history of depression.\n\nUpon further questioning from his general practitioner, the patient reports that he sees no point in eating because he believes himself to be non-existent.\n\nWhat is the correct description of what he is experiencing?",
