      "correctText": "Cotard syndrome",
      "explanation": "Cotard syndrome is characterised by a person believing they are dead or non-existent\n\nCotard syndrome\n\nis correct. This is nihilistic delusional ideation whereby a patient believes they are dead or non-existent. It is associated with depression.\n\nCapgras syndrome\n\n. This is a delusional disorder whereby a patient believes that someone close to them has been replaced by an imposter.\n\nCouvade syndrome\n\nis incorrect. This is also known as a 'sympathetic pregnancy' is a disorder whereby biological fathers suffer the symptoms of pregnancy in the 1st and 3rd trimesters.\n\nDe Clerambault's Syndrome\n\nis incorrect. This is a delusional disorder whereby the patient thinks another person (typically wealthy or famous) is in love with them.\n\nFregoli delusion\n\nis incorrect. This is a delusional disorder whereby the patient believes that different people are in fact the same person in disguise."
