      "id": 108,
      "question": "A 41-year-old man presents to the Emergency Department insisting that he is infested with fleas. He describes that he feels unbearably itchy, and is demanding treatment. This is his third attendance within the last year with this problem. The patient has no significant past medical history and denies taking any recreational drugs. His alcohol intake is reported as 14 units of alcohol per week. He is currently working full-time as a librarian.\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?",
